#!/bin/sh
# ACP agent command for Grimoire started on the handheld (for example from the
# launcher). It hands Grimoire's ACP stdio to the development host's waiting
# grimoire-host-attach session (host/serve-rg-ds-plus), which runs the agent.
# Exits with status 75 when no host session claims it in time.
dir=/run/grimoire-agent
wait_seconds=${GRIMOIRE_HOST_WAIT:-10}
mkdir -p "$dir"
chmod 700 "$dir"
rm -f "$dir/to-host" "$dir/from-host" "$dir/waiting"
mkfifo -m 600 "$dir/to-host" "$dir/from-host"
echo $$ >"$dir/waiting"
# The host session removes the marker when it takes the connection.
tries=$((wait_seconds * 5))
while [ -e "$dir/waiting" ]; do
  tries=$((tries - 1))
  if [ "$tries" -le 0 ]; then
    rm -f "$dir/waiting" "$dir/to-host" "$dir/from-host"
    echo "No development host is connected (start host/serve-rg-ds-plus)." >&2
    exit 75
  fi
  sleep 0.2
done
# Background commands read /dev/null unless stdin is given explicitly.
cat <&0 >"$dir/to-host" &
exec cat <"$dir/from-host"
